CONTRACT FREEZE (A16): docs/MODULE_GUIDE.md v2 and every name listed in module_author_contract are frozen since wave 1; this package must not rename them or change their documented behaviour (additions only; any breaking change needs an architect-approved migration). Module-facing additions (new ctx/core names, fragment schemas, reserved tags) are documented in docs/contract_additions/<this package id>.md, owned by the package that adds them; docs/MODULE_GUIDE.md itself is never edited after the freeze (link fixes by WP29 only). Same-wave sibling names are used exactly as named in this plan (intra-wave protocol, wave-1 goal). 1. v3lum/core/policy.py (new; pure functions, no I/O beyond what PolicyContext carries):
 - Decision (frozen): allowed, status (Status), reason_code (A3 canonical), reason (readable, e.g. 'skipped: noncommercial terms (licence profile corporate)'), rule_id ('POL-01'..), allowed_sources (frozenset|None), emit_manual_link (bool).
 - PolicyContext: options (ScanOptions), config, providers, org (OrgProfile), licence (LicenceState), keys (set of configured key names), now (datetime), quota (QuotaBook|None), health (HealthState|None), offline (bool), explicit (set of module names selected with -M), circuit (set of short-circuited hosts), graph (Graph|None, for the guard), sightings (callable(entity) -> SightingsSummary|None, taken from runtime.meta.get('sightings_lookup'), which App installs from wave 3), path ('scan'|'run'|'shell'|'extract'|'batch'|'watch'|'doctor'). make_context(runtime, options, *, explicit=(), graph=None, path='scan') -> PolicyContext - the ONLY way callers build it (Engine, App.run_single, shell, extract --scan, batch -i, watch, doctor health checks).
 - decide(module_cls, entity, pctx, *, run: RunInfo) -> Decision. First failure wins, in this order (P327 cond 2 preceded by the A3 selection step); every rule id is quoted in the reason:
   POL-01 selection (A3): options.preset == 'quick' and not module.default_enabled and module not in explicit -> SKIPPED 'not_default'; health.is_demoted(module) and not explicit -> SKIPPED 'demoted';
   POL-02 metadata validity (registered v2 module, no load error) -> SKIPPED 'policy';
   POL-03 offline: disclosure in {third_party, internal, target} and offline -> UNAVAILABLE 'offline';
   POL-04 licence (A1/P377): per source: 'open' ok; 'key-terms' ok only if the source's free_plan_business_use is true or config.key_plan(key) == 'business' for the module's key; 'noncommercial'/'license' ok only with an active licence_allow entry, or under the research profile with research_basis covering it; 'unknown' never (every profile); allowed_sources = passing sources; none -> SKIPPED 'licence' (reason 'skipped: <class> terms (licence profile <profile>)', emit_manual_link) - never replaced by a LIGHT/ACTIVE alternative;
   POL-05 TLP (A2, P332 cond 7) with entity TLP = run.tlp or options.tlp: publishes_queries -> SKIPPED 'policy' at any TLP (rule 7); CLEAR/GREEN: everything, unknown tier only with options.allow_unknown; AMBER: excludes unknown tier and reuses_queries; AMBER+STRICT: trusted tier only; RED: disclosure 'none'/'internal' only, plus 'target' on verified own assets that are not third_party_hosted when proxy_light/proxy_active is configured or options.egress_override is set -> otherwise SKIPPED 'tlp';
   POL-06 tier (A8): unknown tier needs options.allow_unknown (recorded) and receives only IOC_TYPES values - never PERSONAL_TYPES, a CNPJ or any other non-IOC type such as keyword or company_name - at any TLP -> SKIPPED 'tier';
   POL-07 privacy (A4/A5/A8/AR16): run_on 'seeds' requires run.is_seed and entity key not in options.unconfirmed_seeds; any PERSONAL_TYPES entity needs options.purpose; a provider without personal_data_review receives PERSONAL_TYPES only when the module is explicit and a purpose is recorded; run_on 'own_assets': e-mail on an org domain that is txt_verified/attested, or options.breach_scope == 'all' + purpose + run.is_seed (never pivots or text-extracted addresses) -> else SKIPPED 'privacy' (reason 'breach check skipped: not an org domain');
   POL-08 own_asset (A11): run_on 'own_assets_only' requires org.owns(entity).verified -> SKIPPED 'own_asset' (reason 'no org profile (v3lum org)' when the profile is empty, printed once by the renderer);
   POL-09 opsec: module.opsec > options.mode -> SKIPPED 'opsec' (no escalation);
   POL-10 rules of engagement (A7): ACTIVE needs a valid options.authorization_ref (regex ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:/#-]{2,63}$, not confirmed/yes/ok/none/n/a/test) -> SKIPPED 'authorization', and options.scope loaded with the same authorization_ref, window open and the entity inside the scope -> SKIPPED 'scope'; LIGHT runs only on analyst-typed seeds (run.is_seed), and without --mode light only on verified own seeds when setting light_for_own_assets is true -> SKIPPED 'scope'; pivots never inherit scope;
   POL-11 egress_country (A9): module.requires_egress not containing setting egress_country -> SKIPPED 'egress_country' (reason 'needs BR egress'), emit_manual_link;
   POL-12 keys: missing requires_keys -> NEEDS_KEY 'needs_key', emit_manual_link;
   POL-13 packages -> UNAVAILABLE 'package';
   POL-14 datasets: a large dataset of the module missing during a scan -> UNAVAILABLE 'dataset';
   POL-15 quota (P334): pctx.quota.exhausted_provider(provider), or the legacy module.daily_quota used up (QuotaBook.exhausted(module, daily_quota)) for providers without a quota block -> QUOTA 'quota', emit_manual_link;
   POL-16 circuit: any module host in pctx.circuit -> BLOCKED 'circuit'.
 - contact_guard(module_cls, entity, pctx, *, run) -> Decision (P376 cond 6-10, A13): only for LIGHT/ACTIVE, evaluated by the engine after the entity's passive results; BLOCKED 'hostile_host' (reason 'needs non-corporate egress') when the entity (or a redirect target) is tagged malicious/phishing/c2/suspicious in the graph or in case-DB sightings, listed by any consensus source (finding tags; CR27 when present), or is hostile-shaped: lookalike of an org brand (org.brand_terms() incl. accent/homoglyph folding), attribute domain_age_days <= 30, lure-word domain (data/brand_lures_pt.json when present), URL/domain whose provenance contains text_blob/file/email_headers; yields only when the profile for its opsec (proxy_light / proxy_active) is configured or options.egress_override is set; the reason lists passive alternatives (urlscan search results, archived copies, sandbox reports), the command `v3lum config set proxy_light socks5h://...` and the override syntax; emit_manual_link.
 - recipient_token(url, org) -> bool (A7 BR15): an org-domain e-mail in plain, URL-encoded or base64 form, or an opaque token of >= 16 chars in path/query.
 - effective_default_set(etype, pctx) -> list[(module_cls, Decision)] and describe_policy(module_cls, pctx) -> list[str] (which policy applies and why; used by `v3lum modules`/`info`, A3/P327 cond 14).
 - RULES: tuple[PolicyRule(id, text, decisions (e.g. ('A1','P377')), test (pytest node id))] covering POL-01..POL-16 and GUARD-01 - the source of docs/RULES.md (AR22); POLICY_VERSION = 'council-1/2026-11-26'.
2. v3lum/core/licence.py: AllowEntry(source_id, basis ('licence'|'provider_grant'|'terms_clause'), scope, legal_ref, approver, decided_at, review_by, evidence_url, quote); ResearchBasis(legal_ref, approver, date, scope); LicenceState.load(path=None) (setting licence_allow_path, default ~/.v3lum/licence_allow.json; looser than 0600 -> warning list; missing -> empty); active(source_id, now) (fail closed: review_by must be >= today and <= decided_at + 12 months); expiring(now, days=30); research_allowed(); resolve_profile(config, options) -> 'corporate'|'research' (LicenceError 'licence_profile=research needs a recorded legal basis (docs/LEGAL.md)' without a research_basis); source_allowed(source, provider, *, key_plan, profile, now) -> (bool, reason).
3. v3lum/core/health.py: HealthState(path=~/.v3lum/health.json, 0600): record_run(module, duration, status), record_votes(module, wrong, total), record_check(module, result), is_demoted(module) per A3 (p50 > 10 s over >= 20 runs; > 30% wrong after >= 10 votes; 3 consecutive failed `doctor --sources` checks; BLOCKED on 5 consecutive runs), notices(), reset(module); a demotion lifts when the condition clears; load/save tolerant of a missing or corrupt file.
4. Review additions: recipient-token URLs (recipient_token(url, org) true) are checked by contact_guard before the hostile-host rules and are never fetched unless the exact URL is in options.confirmed_urls (per-URL confirmation, A7 BR15 / P376 cond 10; --confirm-url in WP13): otherwise SKIPPED 'policy' with reason 'URL carries a per-recipient token: re-run with --confirm-url <url>' (rule GUARD-02) - a configured proxy_light or --egress-override does not lift it, and a confirmed URL still passes the hostile-host checks. Decision gains licence_basis: dict[str, str] (source id -> 'open' | 'business_plan:<key>' | 'allow:<legal_ref>' | 'research:<legal_ref>'), which WP08 copies into case['licence_used'] for the report licence banner and coverage (A1 BR6, P377 cond 5). POL-01 also refuses modules tagged watch_only when pctx.path != 'watch' (SKIPPED 'not_applicable', 'runs only inside v3lum watch'). RULES gains GUARD-02.

